            <ArticleTitle>Clinical care of patients with epidural infusions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1429-32</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Opioids and local anaesthetics are the two main agents used in epidural analgesia. The procedure has many potential side-effects, including hypotension, pruritus, urinary retention, headache and respiratory depression.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
